      "body": "\r\nIssue Type: <b>Bug</b>\r\n\r\nSteps: It is easy to reproduce the bug. Just open the Help menu and click on the \"Open Process Explorer\" button. You will see some gibberish text on the top of the columns. You can see it on the screenshot. The columns aren't even resizable! That's quite bad. Could you fix the gibberish text and add resizable columns in the Process Explorer, please? I would really appreciate.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/70533786/140501679-8872a495-eb80-4a8e-ad26-4d1abb08187a.png)\r\n\r\nVS Code version: Code 1.62.0 (b3318bc0524af3d74034b8bb8a64df0ccf35549a, 2021-11-03T15:23:01.379Z)\r\nOS version: Windows_NT x64 10.0.19043\r\nRestricted Mode: No\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>System Info</summary>\r\n\r\n|Item|Value|\r\n|---|---|\r\n|CPUs|11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1135G7 @ 2.40GHz (8 x 2419)|\r\n|GPU Status|2d_canvas: enabled<br>gpu_compositing: enabled<br>multiple_raster_threads: enabled_on<br>oop_rasterization: enabled<br>opengl: enabled_on<br>rasterization: enabled<br>skia_renderer: enabled_on<br>video_decode: enabled<br>vulkan: disabled_off<br>webgl: enabled<br>webgl2: enabled|\r\n|Load (avg)|undefined|\r\n|Memory (System)|15.80GB (9.39GB free)|\r\n|Process Argv|--crash-reporter-id f667050e-cd55-4c9b-8828-622f51c58fbd|\r\n|Screen Reader|no|\r\n|VM|0%|\r\n</details><details><summary>Extensions (4)</summary>\r\n\r\nExtension|Author (truncated)|Version\r\n---|---|---\r\nvscode-eslint|dba|2.2.2\r\nvscode-language-pack-pl|MS-|1.62.2\r\ncpptools|ms-|1.7.1\r\nmarkdown-preview-enhanced|shd|0.6.1\r\n\r\n\r\n</details><details>\r\n<summary>A/B Experiments</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\nvsliv368cf:30146710\r\nvsreu685:30147344\r\npython383cf:30185419\r\nvspor879:30202332\r\nvspor708:30202333\r\nvspor363:30204092\r\npythontb:30283811\r\npythonvspyt551:30345470\r\npythonptprofiler:30281270\r\nvshan820:30294714\r\nvstes263:30335439\r\npythondataviewer:30285071\r\npythonvsuse255:30340121\r\nvscod805:30301674\r\npy